WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
In 1980, smallpox was declared eradicated.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.720
Its vaccine needed just one dose.

3
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.340
Two doses of measles vaccine have
eliminated measles in many places.

4
00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.090
Yet the flu vaccine is
made new every single year.

5
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.690
Why do some vaccines protect for so long,

6
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.480
while flu needs a new one every year?

7
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.680
In this mission, you'll see
what goes into a vaccine,

8
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.390
from killed microbes to mRNA.

9
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.820
Then you'll follow what a vaccine
sets off inside your body,

10
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.790
without causing the disease.

11
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.670
Your mission: explain why some
vaccines protect for life,

12
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.190
while the flu vaccine changes every year.
